// Title: Disable Windows Firewall by Registry
// Sigma ID: e78c408a-e2ea-43cd-b5ea-51975cf358c0
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-08-19 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1686.003
// Description: Detect set EnableFirewall to 0 to disable the Windows firewall
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/40b77d63808dd4f4eafb83949805636735a1fd15/atomics/T1562.004/T1562.004.md
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_disable_windows_firewall.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (RegistryKey endswith "\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsFirewall\\StandardProfile\\EnableFirewall" or RegistryKey endswith "\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsFirewall\\DomainProfile\\EnableFirewall") and RegistryValueData =~ "DWORD (0x00000000)"
